From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ppe: flow/tunnel fixes for Linux 6.12 and MAP-T shim

Second batch of 6.12 port fixes for the qca-nss-ppe core module:

  ppe_drv_flow.c     vzalloc()/vfree() are implicit without
                     <linux/vmalloc.h>; include it (mainline has the
                     calls, only the header was missing)
  ppe_drv_flow.c     -Wmissing-prototypes (6.10): five helpers used only
                     inside this file and never exported -> static
  ppe_drv_flow.c     dev->priv_flags_ext / IFF_EXT_MAPT do not exist
  tun/ppe_drv_tun_v6.c  in mainline (see below)

Classification:

  mainline equivalent     vmalloc header include
  must shim               priv_flags_ext / IFF_EXT_MAPT

QSDK adds a priv_flags_ext word to struct net_device and sets
IFF_EXT_MAPT on MAP-T interfaces.  Mainline 6.12 has neither field nor
flag, and qca-nss-ppe-mapt is not part of this port, so nothing can ever
set the bit here.  ppe_drv_dev_is_mapt() therefore returns false, which
makes the port behave exactly like a QSDK build without MAP-T rather
than dropping the check.  This is a behavioural shim, not a build fix:
if MAP-T is added later it has to become a real mainline flag.

ppe_tun is built for this target (PPE_TUN_ENABLE=y), which is why
tun/ppe_drv_tun_v6.c is fixed here as well.
